# InputPlumber — the input daemon: reads each board's pad/MCU (devices.d + capability maps) and
# presents one virtual X-Box Elite pad to OpenGamepadUI and every emulator. Built FROM SOURCE via
# the local PKGBUILD since 0.82.0 (a prebuilt.pin on the release tarball before that — see git
# history for the pin and its device-adoption notes); from source because of the patches:
#
#   0001  upstream PR #757 (shadowapex/input-layers-v2, 2026-10-19, based on v0.82.0 exactly):
#         input layers in device profiles. A mapping may target `layer: {name: x}`; while the
#         activating input is held (or latched with mode: toggle) the layer's mappings override
#         the base ones, releases are emitted for whatever the layer produced (no stuck keys),
#         and layers stack. This is the Guide-modifier mechanism for emulator hotkeys
#         (Guide+L1/R1/R2/Start), asked of ShadowApex 2026-10-18, answered with this PR.
#         Drop when a release carries it. An older InputPlumber parses a profile with layers
#         fine and silently ignores them (unknown fields are skipped).
#   0002  ours, upstream PR #771 on top of PR #757 (redesigned 2026-11-07 at ShadowApex's request
#         there): a `layer` target event takes `on_deactivation: {only_when_unused, emit_events}`,
#         tapped (press, then release) when its activator lets the layer go: hold released, toggle
#         pressed again. Guide -> layer guide with on_deactivation ui_guide (only_when_unused) then
#         opens the OGUI menu on a lone tap and stays silent after Guide+R1. Clearing the stack
#         (profile load, device removal, suspend) emits nothing. Replaces the first design (a
#         mapping's other outputs held back until release), so every profile and OGUI 0024 moved
#         ui_guide under the layer target. Drop with 0001 once upstream carries it.
#   0003  ours, split out of the first 0002 (separate upstream PR): a profile load releases what the
#         active layers produced first, as a device removal already does. OGUI loads its focus
#         profile while Guide+South is still held, and the lost ui_quick release made the DBus
#         target drop the next press as a duplicate (quick bar and OSK opened every other time).
#         Independent of 0002; drop once upstream carries it.
#   0004  ours, for upstream: the DBus target thresholds stick and trigger input (a direction or
#         trigger "presses" past 0.60 / 0.75 and releases below), but chose that by the event's own
#         capability, which for a profile-translated event is the DBus one. Since OGUI's focus
#         profile (opengamepadui 0024) maps LeftStick -> ui_left.. and the analog triggers -> ui_l2 /
#         ui_r2, the raw value went out on every change, and OGUI reads only 1.0 as pressed: the
#         stick did not move focus and the analog triggers missed the on-screen keyboard's shift
#         (L2) and enter (R2) nearly always. Goes by the event's source capability now.
name: inputplumber
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
patches: 0001-feat-Input-Layers-add-input-layers-to-map-button-com.patch 0002-feat-Input-Layers-emit-events-when-a-layer-activatio.patch 0003-fix-Input-Layers-release-layer-outputs-before-loadin.patch 0004-fix-DBus-threshold-axis-and-trigger-input-a-profile-translated.patch
pkgrel_suffix: 1
